course: dictionary
lesson: 14214
title: Words about our town
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Municipal is an adjective. It describes something that belongs to a town or city, or is run by its council. The council is the group of people who look after the local area. «The municipal swimming pool opens every day in summer.» Municipal tells you who runs the pool: the town council.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Libraries, parks, bins and pools are all things a council takes care of. So if a sentence is about a library, a park or rubbish collection, municipal may mean run by the council. Check by swapping your meaning in: «The council's library» should still make sense.
explain: Municipal is a formal word, so you will meet it in letters, notices and the news. Learn the phrases too: municipal council, municipal library and municipal elections. When you are not sure, the dictionary settles it.
fact: Municipal means belonging to or run by a town or city council.
fact: A council is a group of people chosen to make decisions for a local area.
fact: «Municipal» is a formal word, so you will often see it on signs, letters and in the news.
fact: Municipal services include libraries, parks, rubbish collection and swimming pools.
fact: Phrases to know: municipal council, municipal library, municipal elections.
exercise: «The municipal library lends books for free.» Who runs the library? | A school | Each family on the street | A supermarket chain | *A town or city council
exercise: Which of these is a municipal service? | *Collecting rubbish from every street | A private shop selling shoes | A family's garden hedge | A football club's training ground
exercise: What does municipal mean? | Loud and noisy | Belonging to one family only | Very old and dusty | *Belonging to or run by a town or city council
test: «The municipal swimming pool opens at nine.» What does municipal tell you about the pool? | Run by a famous swimmer | *Run by the town council | Full of sea water | Only open in winter
test: Which phrase is about local elections for the council? | Ancient castle | *Municipal elections | Glum face | Curt reply
exam: «The municipal park has new benches.» Which best explains municipal here? | The park is very old and ruined | The park is under the sea | The park is a private garden owned by one family | *The park is looked after by the town council
